id: decisions/052-credit-the-whole-lineage
title: "Credit every named author, not just the lead"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'credit-reach'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: credit-reach
axis_gloss: "how far back credit is carried: every upstream influence named, or credit stopped at the immediate author"
poles:
  a: bounded-self-credit
  b: full-lineage-credit
split: lone-exception
draft_status: full
leverage: 1.4
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(3) x split_weight(0.4) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  When YAWN borrows an idea, must every named author of the source be credited
  wherever the idea appears, or is naming the lead author on the page enough if
  the full list lives in the record?

why_it_matters: >
  references/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_RESEARCH_BRAID.yawn authors
  attribution_precedes_extension: true, and
  core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn warns in section 16.1 against
  implying Vervaeke alone authored the framework, yet the same document's
  completion checklist requires only visible Vervaeke attribution on the arena
  page. Once answered, a bot that renders a public page or a child Yawn that
  extends a borrowed frame knows the minimum credit it must carry and where the
  full lineage has to be reachable from.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    1 judgments sit at bounded-self-credit (0 authored) and 2 at
    full-lineage-credit (1 authored). The repository asserts both directions on
    this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave regards an external service (service:supabase in
    examples/waiting-turn.yawn) as a party that is credited as an arena
    participant or as a tool; the extraction filed that under this axis and it is
    really a separate question.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: A visible surface credits the lead author or tradition; the full author
      list lives in the source record's front matter (inspired_in_part_by with
      authors, work, year, DOI) and is reachable by link. Section 20's checklist
      item stands as written.
    cost: "None to the tree; one sentence in section 16.1 conceding that the page may name the lead author alone."
    risk: "The page does exactly what section 16.1 says not to do, and readers who never follow the link take the lead author for the sole author."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "None beyond the existing front-matter; a test could only assert that the ARENA record carries inspired_in_part_by, which it does."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0195"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: Every surface that presents a borrowed framing carries the full author
      list as the source record states it, and attribution precedes extension
      everywhere. No page, README, or rendered View may name fewer authors than the
      record it draws on.
    cost: "Rewrites the section 20 checklist item and docs/research-basis.md; every future public surface carries two full author lists."
    risk: "Long attribution blocks crowd the 'quiet host entry' the chrome contract requires, and public_root prohibits explanatory header copy."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "New tests/attribution-lineage.test.mjs: for each record with inspired_in_part_by, every public surface that cites it (ARENA section 20, docs/research-basis.md, README.md) contains each author name; today the checklist item fails."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0412"
      - "J0663"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: Full lineage lives in the record (front matter with authors, work, year,
      DOI; attribution_precedes_extension: true; an attribution_boundary stating
      that none of the named authors endorse YAWN). A rendered surface carries at
      least the lead author and the year for each borrowed work plus a visible link
      to the lineage record, and may never phrase the credit so as to imply sole
      authorship. Section 20's checklist item is rewritten to name both works with
      their lead authors and to link section 16.1.
    cost: "One checklist line, one line in docs/research-basis.md, one sentence in references/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_RESEARCH_BRAID.yawn synthesis_contract."
    risk: "'Implies sole authorship' is a judgment call only a human can make, so the test can check names and links but not phrasing."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "New tests/attribution-lineage.test.mjs: every public surface citing a record with inspired_in_part_by names each work's lead author and year and links to the record; phrasing is listed under proof.human_review_required in the ARENA record."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0663"
      - "J0195"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.65
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    The authored rule is on the full-lineage side, and the lone exception is a
    checklist line inside the very document that authored the warning against it,
    so this is a self-contradiction within one file rather than a considered
    carve-out. B is the pure form but collides with the chrome contract's
    quiet-root rule and the public_root prohibition on explanatory copy, both of
    which are test-pinned; C keeps the full list in the record, the link on the
    page, and forbids the phrasing section 16.1 already forbids. J0412 (an
    external service listed as an arena participant) is a weak fit for this axis
    and is resolved here only in the sense that C does not bear on it.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn section 20 checklist names both works with lead authors and year and links section 16.1."
    - "docs/research-basis.md carries the same credit and a link to the lineage record."
    - "A test in tests/ asserts the names and links on every public surface citing a lineage record, and the phrasing check is listed under human_review_required."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A public page credits Vervaeke alone, or extends a borrowed frame without
    naming its source, after ratification and no test fails.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0195"
  - "J0412"
  - "J0663"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  id_index: TAXONOMY.md
